  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental lines from Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances - Governmental Funds, Total column (p4); Taxes, State receipts and Local receipts were split into the lines printed on the all-funds schedule (p8; General + Street columns, tying to 153,090 / 91,520 / 100,421). Motor vehicle fees (4,590, printed under State receipts) categorized as motor vehicle tax. Business-type lines from the proprietary statement (p6-7); the Utilities fund is the Enterprise Fund; its Other income 4,017 split into Miscellaneous 3,767 + Fees and permits 250 per p8. Utility debt service principal/interest are nonoperating expenditures recorded as disbursements. Business-type measure is cash (modified cash basis). Transfers: General (15,000) out, Street 15,000 in, net zero in total column. Roll-forwards: governmental 201,540 + 345,031 - 301,179 + 15,000 - 15,000 = 245,392; business-type 616,125 + 220,363 - 330,312 = 506,176. Balance sheet = Total column of the net position section of the Statement of Activities and Net Position (p2); no liabilities reported. Budget-basis schedule (p10, combined all funds by function, with budget figures) not recorded in detail to avoid double counting with the per-fund schedule on p8-9; its actuals tie (revenues 565,394, expenditures 631,491). Business-type receipts total is the Utilities column of the revenue schedule (p8). Read pages 1-10 of 10"
}